# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/intro.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event intro_welcome
# en: The Welcome
title [ac6c10] = 欢迎仪式
# en: Floating candles, two hundred first-years trying not to look up. Headmistress Marrow speaks for four minutes: four years of twelve moons, a name that travels, and a castle that remembers who you were in it. "Before you choose your courses," she ends, "the prefects will show you how things work here. Those who think they know already may go straight to the registrar."
text [e809d0] = 漂浮的蜡烛，两百个一年级新生努力不抬头看。马罗院长讲了四分钟：四年，每年十二个月，一个会传开的名字，还有一座会记住你在这里是什么样的人的城堡。“在你们选课之前，”她最后说，“级长们会带你们看看这里的规矩。自认为已经知道的人，可以直接去找教务。”
# en: The Great Hall full of new first-years under floating candles, a tall headmistress at the lectern.
scene [a752a8] = 大礼堂里挤满了新来的一年级生，头顶飘着蜡烛，高个子的院长站在讲台前。
# en: Skip the orientation
opt.left.label [7bb86b] = 跳过入学引导
# en: You slip out ahead of the crowd to find the registrar's list. Whatever the castle has to teach you, you'll learn it the hard way. (The safety talk is compulsory: you'll still have that.)
opt.left.say.1 [c27814] = 你赶在人群前头溜出去找教务的名单。城堡要教你的东西，你打算用吃苦头的方式学。（安全课是必修的：那个你还是得上。）
# en: Stay for the orientation
opt.right.label [b7a0f6] = 留下参加引导
# en: You stay. The hall empties toward the prefects, and the headmistress comes down from the lectern, straight toward you.
opt.right.say.1 [88c52b] = 你留了下来。大厅里的人朝级长们散去，院长从讲台上走下来，径直朝你走来。

@event intro_what_is_just
# en: What Is Just?
title [ebf19a] = 何为公正？
# en: Headmistress Marrow stops in front of you, notebook open, as if she'd been looking for you in particular. "One question before the prefects have you," she says. "I ask it of everyone. Very few remember. What do you think is just?"
text [f37f9c] = 马罗院长在你面前停下，笔记本摊开着，好像特意在找你。“在级长们把你领走之前，问一个问题，”她说，“我问每一个人。记得的人很少。你觉得什么是公正？”
# en: A tall headmistress with a small notebook stopping in front of one first-year in an emptying hall, candles guttering overhead.
scene [bd9664] = 渐空的大厅里，一位高个子的院长拿着小笔记本，停在一个一年级生面前，头顶的蜡烛摇曳将熄。
# en: "Mercy."
opt.mercy.label [715ccb] = “仁慈。”
# en: Giving people more than they've earned.
opt.mercy.hint [18f8eb] = 给人超过他们应得的。
# en: "Mercy," she repeats, and writes it down. "Expensive. Most people who say it haven't been asked to pay for it yet." She closes the notebook on her finger. "Ask me again in four years."
opt.mercy.say.1 [87a6e2] = “仁慈，”她重复一遍，写了下来。“代价高昂。说这话的人大多还没被要求付账。”她用手指夹住笔记本合上。“四年后再问我一次。”
# en: "Fairness."
opt.fair.label [a659a4] = “公平。”
# en: One rule, the same for everyone.
opt.fair.hint [0a96a2] = 一条规矩，对谁都一样。
# en: "Fairness," she repeats, and writes it down. "The same rule for the duke and the pickpocket. Harder than it sounds, when you know one of them." She closes the notebook on her finger. "Ask me again in four years."
opt.fair.say.1 [73d120] = “公平，”她重复一遍，写了下来。“公爵和扒手守同一条规矩。等你认识其中一个，就知道这比听上去难。”她用手指夹住笔记本合上。“四年后再问我一次。”
# en: "Keeping your own safe."
opt.strong.label [ae02c4] = “护住自己人。”
# en: Whatever it takes, for the people who are yours.
opt.strong.hint [02410d] = 为了属于你的人，不惜一切。
# en: "Keeping your own safe," she repeats, and writes it down. "An honest answer. Most people dress it up." She closes the notebook on her finger. "Ask me again in four years. I'd like to know who you decided was yours."
opt.strong.say.1 [4caa6c] = “护住自己人，”她重复一遍，写了下来。“很诚实的回答。大多数人会粉饰一番。”她用手指夹住笔记本合上。“四年后再问我一次。我想知道你最后认定谁是你的人。”

@event intro_tour
# en: The Prefect's Tour
title [5bfdbd] = 级长带你参观
# en: A burly prefect in a red sash gathers the first-years with a ledger. "Bram Hollis. Prefect. Tour. Each day you get a few free hours, and you spend them on the map: one place an hour. Some doors open only once you've earned them. Some never open for you. Keep up."
text [d68b57] = 一个魁梧的、系红肩带的级长拿着账本召集一年级生。“布拉姆·霍利斯。级长。参观。每天你有几个空闲时段，在地图上花掉它们：一个时段去一个地方。有些门要等你配得上才会开。有些门永远不会为你开。跟上。”
# en: A prefect in a red sash leading a straggle of first-years through a castle corridor, holding up a ledger like a flag.
scene [99ab49] = 一个系红肩带的级长领着一串一年级生穿过城堡走廊，像举旗一样举着账本。
# en: Skip the tour
opt.left.label [e05505] = 不参观了
# en: You slip away and find your own way round. You get lost twice and find the kitchens once, which is a fair trade.
opt.left.say.1 [d82ebc] = 你溜走了，自己摸路。迷路两次，找到厨房一次，挺划算。
# en: Follow him round
opt.right.label [3e4916] = 跟着他转
# en: Bram walks you past every door and names its rules. At a blank stretch of wall, a boy with a lockpick behind his ear winks at you, as if the wall were a joke you'd both get later.
opt.right.say.1 [3f75b9] = 布拉姆领你走过每一扇门，说出每一扇门的规矩。在一段光秃秃的墙前，一个耳后夹着撬锁针的男孩冲你眨了眨眼，好像这堵墙是个你们俩以后都会懂的笑话。

@event intro_places
# en: Where Things Are
title [168cb7] = 东西都在哪儿
# en: Bram reads the castle to you off his ledger. "Job Board, by the stairs: work and wages. Library: revision tables before every exam. Infirmary, on the Alchemy floor: Sister Amaranth, for when you break something, yourself included. The village, down the hill: robes and wands on market day, tea at Mabel's, tonics at Pell's." He snaps the ledger shut. "Questions? No. Good."
text [dceb2a] = 布拉姆照着账本把城堡念给你听。“招工告示板，在楼梯边：活儿和工钱。图书馆：每次考试前都摆好复习桌。医务室，在炼金那层：阿玛兰斯修女，摔坏了什么都找她，包括你自己。村子，在山下：集市日买长袍和魔杖，梅布尔茶馆喝茶，佩尔父女药铺买补剂。”他啪地合上账本。“有问题吗？没有。很好。”
# en: A prefect reading from a ledger at the top of a castle stair, pointing down corridors with his quill, first-years craning to follow.
scene [b6f58c] = 城堡楼梯顶上，一个级长照着账本念，用羽毛笔朝各条走廊指点，一年级生伸长脖子跟着看。
# en: "No questions."
opt.left.label [e3ca6b] = “没有问题。”
# en: "Excellent," says Bram, and means it. He leaves you at the foot of the stairs with a map in your head and a strong sense of having been processed.
opt.left.say.1 [90461f] = “好极了，”布拉姆说，是真心的。他把你丢在楼梯底下，脑子里多了张地图，还有一种被办完了手续的强烈感觉。
# en: Ask what he left out
opt.right.label [23dbe0] = 问他漏了什么
# en: He looks pained. "The Gilded Newt, in the village, after dark: supper, cider and people you shouldn't be seen with. The Lakeshore, for thinking. That's all." He writes something in the ledger. It might be your name.
opt.right.say.1 [bbe3ed] = 他一脸痛苦。“镀金蝾螈酒馆，在村里，天黑以后：晚饭、苹果酒，还有你不该被人看见跟他们在一起的人。湖岸，想事情用的。就这些。”他在账本上写了点什么。可能是你的名字。

@event intro_wrong_tower
# en: The Wrong Tower
title [658cc8] = 走错的塔楼
# en: Your trunk has gone to the wrong tower. The house steward has a list, and the list says it hasn't. "If it's on the list," she says, "it's where it should be." Behind her, through a door, you can see your trunk with your name on it.
text [2251e2] = 你的箱子被送到了错的塔楼。舍监手里有一张名单，名单上说没送错。“名单上怎么写，东西就在哪儿，”她说。在她身后，透过一扇门，你能看见写着你名字的箱子。
# en: A harassed house steward behind a desk heaped with lists, a student's trunk visible through a doorway in the wrong tower.
scene [91c6b6] = 一位手忙脚乱的舍监坐在堆满名单的桌后，透过门口能看见错的塔楼里有一个学生的箱子。
# en: Carry it over yourself
opt.left.label [a8f8c6] = 自己搬过去
# en: You haul it across two bridges and up ninety stairs. The steward ticks something on the list as you pass, satisfied that it was always right.
opt.left.say.1 [246fa2] = 你拖着它过了两座桥，爬了九十级台阶。你经过时，舍监在名单上打了个勾，满意地认为它一直都是对的。
# en: Talk her round
opt.right.label [53212c] = 说服她
# en: A negotiation, as a lesson: a fair chance, and nothing more than your mood at stake. Until the negotiation game arrives, charm, lore and guile decide it.
opt.right.hint [cfeefd] = 一场交涉，当作一课：机会对半，赌上的只有你的心情。在交涉小游戏上线之前，由魅力、学识和诡计决定。
# en: You ask to see the list. Then the line. Then the tower on the line. The steward goes pink, corrects it in red ink and sends two porters. "Clerical," she says.
opt.right.say.1 [f54cdc] = 你要求看名单。然后看那一行。然后看那一行写的是哪座塔。舍监脸红了，用红墨水改过来，派了两个搬运工。“笔误，”她说。
# en: She won't change the list, but she lends you a porter "as a courtesy". The porter and the list never speak again.
opt.right.say.2 [2de114] = 她不肯改名单，但“出于礼貌”借给你一个搬运工。搬运工和名单从此再没说过话。
# en: She has an answer for everything, most of it the list. You carry the trunk yourself in the end, but you've learned how she argues, which is worth a tower.
opt.right.say.3 [d9aebe] = 她什么都有理由，大部分理由就是那张名单。最后你还是自己搬了箱子，但你学会了她怎么争论，这值一座塔。

@event intro_lunch
# en: The Lunch Table
title [a7afb4] = 午餐桌
# en: Lunch in the Great Hall, under the gallery where the refectory tables run. You can sit anywhere. At noon people find you, or you find them; either way, who you sit with tends to become who you know.
text [b43e18] = 大礼堂里的午餐，膳堂的长桌摆在楼廊底下。你可以随便坐。中午，别人会找到你，或者你找到别人；不管怎样，你跟谁坐在一起，往往就会认识谁。
# en: Long refectory tables at noon, first-years spread along the benches, one empty place beside a familiar face.
scene [319811] = 中午的膳堂长桌，一年级生沿着长凳散坐，一张熟悉的脸旁边空着一个位子。
# en: Eat with whoever's there
opt.left.label [99acdb] = 随便跟旁边的人吃
# en: You squeeze in between two strangers who are arguing about soup. By pudding they're not strangers, quite.
opt.left.say.1 [5284d5] = 你挤进两个正为汤争论的陌生人中间。吃到布丁时，他们已经不太算陌生人了。
# en: Sit with {friend}
opt.right.label [c9b8a7] = 和{friend}坐在一起
# en: {friend} shifts along the bench to make room. You talk about nothing much, which is how most friendships start.
opt.right.say.1 [2dae0b] = {friend}在长凳上挪了挪给你让位子。你们聊了些没什么要紧的事，大多数友谊就是这么开始的。

@event intro_lunch_alone
# en: The Lunch Table
title [a7afb4] = 午餐桌
# en: Lunch in the Great Hall, under the gallery where the refectory tables run. You can sit anywhere, and you don't know anyone yet. At noon people find you, or you find them; either way, who you sit with tends to become who you know.
text [0a4985] = 大礼堂里的午餐，膳堂的长桌摆在楼廊底下。你可以随便坐，而你还谁都不认识。中午，别人会找到你，或者你找到别人；不管怎样，你跟谁坐在一起，往往就会认识谁。
# en: Long refectory tables at noon, first-years spread along the benches, a student with a tray looking for a place.
scene [93647d] = 正午膳堂的长桌，一年级生沿长凳散坐，一个端着餐盘的学生在找位子。
# en: Eat with whoever's there
opt.left.label [99acdb] = 随便跟旁边的人吃
# en: You squeeze in between two strangers who are arguing about soup. By pudding they're not strangers, quite.
opt.left.say.1 [5284d5] = 你挤进两个正为汤争论的陌生人中间。吃到布丁时，他们已经不太算陌生人了。
# en: Sit at the end and listen
opt.right.label [981f2a] = 坐到桌尾听着
# en: You take the end of a bench and listen. By the end of the meal you know who runs the Ledger, who duels, who talks to plants, and that the girl with the floating quill will find you whether you like it or not.
opt.right.say.1 [27bcdf] = 你在长凳尽头坐下，听着。一顿饭吃完，你已经知道谁在办《纪事报》、谁决斗、谁跟植物说话，还知道那个羽毛笔浮在肩头的女孩迟早会找上你，不管你愿不愿意。

@event intro_vey_tea
# en: Tea That Isn't There
title [52dadd] = 不存在的茶
# en: Professor Vey stops you in a corridor and offers you a cup of tea. There is no cup. There is no tea. She waits to see what you'll do. "Every attempt has its odds," she says pleasantly. "Skill moves them. Luck moves them less. Drink up."
text [747e3f] = 维伊教授在走廊里拦住你，请你喝一杯茶。没有杯子。没有茶。她等着看你怎么做。“每次尝试都有它的胜算，”她和气地说，“本事能改变胜算。运气改变得少一点。喝吧。”
# en: A corridor alcove, a sharp-eyed professor holding out an empty hand as if it held a teacup, a student hesitating.
scene [8c672c] = 走廊的壁龛里，一位目光锐利的教授伸着一只空手，好像端着茶杯，一个学生犹豫着。
# en: Decline the tea
opt.left.label [5a06b4] = 谢绝这杯茶
# en: "No, thank you," you say. Vey sighs, drinks the tea that isn't there, and walks on. You feel as though you've failed something small.
opt.left.say.1 [c1f092] = “不了，谢谢，”你说。维伊叹了口气，喝掉了那杯不存在的茶，走开了。你觉得自己好像没通过一件小事。
# en: Pretend to drink it
opt.right.label [603f5b] = 假装喝下去
# en: A check, as a lesson: your guile, a fair chance, and nothing more than your mood at stake.
opt.right.hint [c2e062] = 一次检定，当作一课：凭你的诡计，机会对半，赌上的只有你的心情。
# en: You sip, wince at the heat and compliment the blend. Vey laughs, delighted, and writes something down. "Points," she says. "Nobody compliments the blend."
opt.right.say.1 [bb798d] = 你抿了一口，被烫得皱眉，夸了夸茶的配方。维伊高兴地笑了，写下了什么。“得分，”她说，“从没人夸过配方。”
# en: You drink it convincingly and then try to hand back the cup. There is no cup. Vey smiles. "Half points," she says.
opt.right.say.2 [f5309d] = 你喝得很像样，然后想把杯子递回去。没有杯子。维伊笑了。“半分，”她说。
# en: You laugh halfway through the sip. Vey sighs, theatrically. "Most do," she says. "I keep score, you know. Everyone starts at nought."
opt.right.say.3 [40b8ab] = 你喝到一半笑了出来。维伊夸张地叹了口气。“大多数人都这样，”她说，“我会记分的，你知道吧。每个人都从零开始。”

@event intro_purse
# en: The Purse
title [d2b797] = 钱袋
# en: Your purse is lighter than it was: the bursar has taken this month's board, as he will every month. Among the coins is a calling card in green ink. "GRISK. Loans on friendly terms. Ask at the Newt."
text [e8b293] = 你的钱袋比以前轻了：总务收走了这个月的伙食费，以后每个月都会收。硬币中间有一张绿墨水写的名片。“格里斯克。友善条件放贷。到蝾螈酒馆找我。”
# en: A student counting coins out of a small purse onto a dormitory blanket, a goblin's calling card among them.
scene [01fe67] = 一个学生在宿舍的毯子上从小钱袋里数硬币，其中夹着一张地精的名片。
# en: Pocket it
opt.left.label [2cf130] = 收起来
# en: You put the card away with the coins and decide to be careful. It is a good decision, for now.
opt.left.say.1 [90ded8] = 你把名片和硬币收在一起，决定小心些。这个决定，暂时是对的。
# en: Read Grisk's card
opt.right.label [ad3369] = 读格里斯克的名片
# en: Sixty crowns today, the back says, and twelve a month for six months. The arithmetic is very friendly indeed, to Grisk.
opt.right.say.1 [5d83c2] = 背面写着：今天借六十克朗，之后六个月每月还十二。这笔账确实非常友善——对格里斯克来说。

@event intro_room
# en: Your Room
title [d2c355] = 你的房间
# en: Your room in the tower: a bed, a trunk, a window with half the lake in it. On the pillow, a note from the bursar, folded twice.
text [be66cd] = 你在塔楼里的房间：一张床，一只箱子，一扇装着半个湖的窗。枕头上有一张总务写的字条，折了两折。
# en: A narrow tower room with a bed, a trunk at its foot and a window full of lake, a folded note on the pillow.
scene [efd3ce] = 一间窄窄的塔楼房间，一张床，床脚一只箱子，窗外满是湖水，枕头上一张折好的字条。
# en: Unpack later
opt.left.label [5dce1d] = 晚点再收拾
# en: You fall onto the bed in your robes and sleep like a dropped stone. The note is still under your cheek in the morning.
opt.left.say.1 [053903] = 你穿着袍子倒在床上，睡得像块落地的石头。第二天早上，字条还压在你脸颊下。
# en: Read the bursar's note
opt.right.label [aec687] = 读总务的字条
# en: Board is paid each month, it says, or you go hungry. Sleep mends the body and the mood; a bad night shows. Mana comes back on its own. And please do not feed the gargoyles.
opt.right.say.1 [fc0300] = 上面说，伙食费每月交，不交就挨饿。睡眠能修复身体和心情；没睡好会看出来。法力会自己回来。另外请不要喂石像鬼。

@event intro_practice_circle
# en: The Practice Circle
title [635caf] = 练习圈
# en: Professor Thorne has chalked a circle and stood a straw mannequin in it. "Every first-year fights it once," he says. "It moves first, and it shows you what it means to do. Watch it. Lose to it if you must. Losing well is the only thing worth teaching."
text [dd8433] = 索恩教授用粉笔画了一个圈，在里面立了一个稻草假人。“每个一年级生都要跟它打一次，”他说，“它先出招，而且会让你看到它想干什么。看着它。必要的话就输给它。输得漂亮，是唯一值得教的东西。”
# en: A chalk circle on a scorched duelling-hall floor, a straw mannequin standing in it, a grizzled professor watching from the edge.
scene [f32b3e] = 焦黑的决斗厅地板上画着粉笔圈，圈里立着一个稻草假人，一位头发花白的教授在圈边看着。
# en: Watch from the bench
opt.left.label [ff2b65] = 在长椅上看
# en: You watch three first-years go down to the mannequin, then one beat it. Thorne says the same thing to all four: "Good. Again."
opt.left.say.1 [5db4f2] = 你看着三个一年级生倒在假人面前，然后一个打赢了。索恩对四个人说的都是同一句话：“好。再来。”
# en: Step into the circle
opt.right.label [7ce474] = 走进圈里
# en: A lesson: Thorne talks you through every exchange, and only your mood is at stake.
opt.right.hint [dae7e9] = 一课：每个回合索恩教授都会指点你，赌上的只有你的心情。
# en: The mannequin topples in a puff of straw. Thorne nods. "Now lose one sometime," he says. "Then you'll know what you're doing."
opt.right.say.1 [9491b1] = 假人扑的一声倒下，扬起一阵稻草。索恩点点头。“找时间输一场，”他说，“那你才知道自己在干什么。”
# en: You trade blows until the bell. Thorne looks pleased. "A draw is a fight you both learned from," he says.
opt.right.say.2 [e70a65] = 你们来回交手直到下课铃响。索恩看起来很满意。“平局就是两边都学到东西的一场打斗，”他说。
# en: The mannequin wins, which is humiliating and educational. Thorne helps you up. "I lost to a storm once," he says. "Badly. Losing well is the whole art."
opt.right.say.3 [522c58] = 假人赢了，这既丢脸又有教育意义。索恩把你扶起来。“我输给过一场风暴，”他说，“输得很惨。输得漂亮，就是全部的本事。”

@event intro_kit
# en: What You Carry
title [14863b] = 随身之物
# en: Afterwards Thorne taps your borrowed wand with one finger. "Held together with hope," he says. "What you carry matters in a fight, and only there: a wand, a robe, one thing in your pocket. What you own opens other doors. Keep your kit in order."
text [56c4a3] = 之后，索恩用一根手指敲了敲你借来的魔杖。“全靠希望撑着，”他说，“你带的东西在打斗里才有用，也只在那里有用：一根魔杖，一件长袍，口袋里的一样东西。你拥有的东西会打开别的门。把你的行装打理好。”
# en: A grizzled professor tapping a student's battered borrowed wand, a robe and a small pouch laid out on a bench.
scene [e32613] = 一位头发花白的教授敲着学生那根破旧的借用魔杖，长凳上摆着一件长袍和一个小袋子。
# en: Later
opt.left.label [f62b49] = 以后再说
# en: You nod and put the wand away. It sparks once, sideways, as if it had heard.
opt.left.say.1 [a6841a] = 你点点头，把魔杖收起来。它往旁边冒了一下火花，好像听见了。
# en: Show me
opt.right.label [4e9f5a] = 给我看看
# en: He shows you: what you wear only counts when you fight; what you own lets you do things on the right day, like a spell does. Your kit is on its own tab, beside the others. "And trade that wand in," he says, "when you can."
opt.right.say.1 [008a04] = 他给你看：穿戴的东西只在打斗时算数；拥有的东西能让你在合适的日子做些事，就像咒语一样。你的行装在单独的标签页里，就在其他标签旁边。“还有，那根魔杖，”他说，“有机会就换掉。”

@event jit_after_curfew
# en: After Curfew
title [0fdaf7] = 宵禁之后
# en: After curfew the castle changes hands. The corridors belong to prefects and to whatever else walks them. You can stay in and sleep, or slip out at midnight to wherever is open then. Get caught often enough and people start to notice.
text [dd6308] = 宵禁之后，城堡换了主人。走廊属于级长，也属于其他在走廊里游荡的东西。你可以待在房里睡觉，也可以在午夜溜出去，去那时还开着的地方。被抓得多了，人们就会开始注意你。
# en: A dark castle corridor after curfew, a prefect's lantern far off at one end, a student pressed into a doorway.
scene [fae1e0] = 宵禁后黑暗的城堡走廊，远处一头有一盏级长的提灯，一个学生贴在门洞里。
# en: Stay in tonight
opt.left.label [1ab842] = 今晚待在房里
# en: You listen to the castle settle and decide midnight can wait.
opt.left.say.1 [e24a2a] = 你听着城堡慢慢安静下来，决定午夜可以等等。
# en: Watch the prefect's lantern go by
opt.right.label [984529] = 看着级长的提灯经过
# en: The lantern passes your door, pauses and moves on. You learn the round by heart. It feels like knowing a secret.
opt.right.say.1 [c313f1] = 提灯经过你的门口，停了一下，又走了。你把巡夜路线记得一清二楚。感觉像是知道了一个秘密。

@event jit_red_string
# en: Red String
title [b7fb15] = 红线
# en: You've started keeping what you notice: a scrap of paper here, a remembered word there. Tonight you pin them to the wall above your desk and join them with red string. It doesn't make sense yet. It isn't supposed to.
text [a4cca7] = 你开始记下自己注意到的东西：这里一张纸条，那里一句记住的话。今晚你把它们钉在书桌上方的墙上，用红线连起来。现在还说不通。本来也不该说得通。
# en: A student's desk by candlelight, scraps of paper pinned to the wall above it, joined by lengths of red string.
scene [ee5fd5] = 烛光下学生的书桌，上方墙上钉着纸片，用一段段红线连在一起。
# en: Go to bed
opt.left.label [2fa817] = 去睡觉
# en: You leave the string where it is. In the morning it looks like a constellation you don't know the name of.
opt.left.say.1 [be60a4] = 你让红线留在那儿。早上看，它像一个你叫不出名字的星座。
# en: Stare at it a while
opt.right.label [3f9d74] = 盯着看一会儿
# en: The things you've found are all there in your notes now, and the leads you haven't followed. Nobody will make you follow them. That's the frightening part.
opt.right.say.1 [39ac5e] = 你发现的东西现在都记在笔记里了，还有你没追下去的线索。没人会逼你去追。这才是可怕的地方。

@event jit_exam_nerves
# en: Exam Nerves
title [a019fb] = 考前紧张
# en: Exams. Outside the hall someone is reciting the stirring count under their breath. Every class you went to and every night you revised is in your head somewhere, and how much of it is there is most of what decides the paper.
text [a5b31c] = 考试。考场外有人在低声背搅拌的次数。你上过的每一节课、复习过的每一个晚上都在你脑子里某处，而还剩下多少，基本就决定了这张卷子。
# en: A queue of pale first-years outside a closed examination hall door, one of them reciting under their breath.
scene [ee9c1f] = 一群脸色发白的一年级生在紧闭的考场门外排队，其中一个在低声背诵。
# en: Walk straight in
opt.left.label [566c0d] = 直接走进去
# en: You walk in before the nerves can catch you. The door shuts like a held breath.
opt.left.say.1 [52c3cc] = 你趁紧张还没追上就走了进去。门关上了，像屏住的一口气。
# en: Go over your notes once more
opt.right.label [a8cb0d] = 再看一遍笔记
# en: Preparation counts more than talent here, a fourth-year once told you. You hope she was right. She usually is.
opt.right.say.1 [2d8c31] = 准备比天赋更重要，一个四年级生曾这么告诉你。你希望她说得对。她通常是对的。

@event jit_long_break
# en: The Long Break
title [66ec9d] = 长假
# en: The term is over and the castle empties. {off_campus: You watch it go from the barge rail, your trunk at your feet.|} A break is your own: no lectures, and four free visits a day if you stay at the castle or go home, three if you take on paid work. Some friends leave; some stay. Letters come instead.
text [75d834] = 学期结束了，城堡空了下来。{off_campus: 你站在驳船栏杆边看着它远去，箱子就在脚边。|}假期是你自己的：没有课，如果留在城堡或者回家，每天有四个空闲时段；如果去打工，就是三个。有些朋友走了，有些留下。信件取而代之。
# en: An emptying castle courtyard, trunks being loaded onto a barge, a few students waving and a few staying behind.
scene [a85881] = 渐渐空下来的城堡庭院，箱子被搬上驳船，几个学生在挥手，几个留了下来。
# en: Make plans later
opt.left.label [ce1835] = 以后再计划
# en: {off_campus: You put your feet up for an afternoon first. Home is very quiet after the castle, and nobody rings a bell at you.|You put your feet up for an afternoon first. The castle is very quiet, and very much yours.}
opt.left.say.1 [90e8ec] = {off_campus: 你先把脚翘起来歇了一个下午。离开城堡，家里安静极了，也没有钟声冲你响。|你先把脚翘起来歇了一个下午。城堡非常安静，完完全全是你的。}
# en: {off_campus: Walk round home|Walk the empty halls}
opt.right.label [2cb97b] = {off_campus: 在家里转转|在空荡荡的大厅里走走}
# en: {off_campus: Everything is smaller than you remember. Your old room is full of apples now, and someone has kept your bed made anyway.|Your footsteps echo. The kitchens are open all day on a break, the cook says, and the cook is lonely.}
opt.right.say.1 [21cdea] = {off_campus: 一切都比你记得的要小。你原来的房间现在堆满了苹果，可还是有人把你的床铺得整整齐齐。|你的脚步声回荡着。厨师说，假期里厨房整天开着，而厨师很寂寞。}

@event jit_counter
# en: Across the Counter
title [abe25b] = 柜台那边
# en: The village sells what the castle doesn't. Every shop has its counter, with its prices on the slate; some things are only offered once you've proved something, or know someone, or can pay a great deal. And the pawnbroker buys back what you're tired of.
text [d74b4b] = 村子卖城堡里没有的东西。每家店都有柜台，价钱写在石板上；有些东西只有在你证明了什么、认识了谁，或者付得起一大笔钱时才会拿出来。当铺还会收你厌倦了的东西。
# en: A village shop counter seen from a student's side, a price slate, a few goods and a shopkeeper waiting patiently.
scene [d6bed1] = 从学生这边看过去的村店柜台，一块价目石板，几样商品，店主在耐心等着。
# en: Browse another day
opt.left.label [a6f176] = 改天再逛
# en: You walk the square with your hands in your pockets. Everything in the windows looks expensive and possible.
opt.left.say.1 [723a4c] = 你双手插兜在广场上转了一圈。橱窗里的一切看起来都很贵，也都很可能。
# en: Read every slate
opt.right.label [4f5893] = 把每块石板都读一遍
# en: Buns, robes, wands, tea, tonics, one at a time. You make a list of what you'd buy if you had money. It's a long list.
opt.right.say.1 [2428e0] = 面包、长袍、魔杖、茶、补剂，一次一种。你列了一张有钱就买的清单。清单很长。

@event jit_real_fight
# en: A Real Fight
title [725eee] = 真正的打斗
# en: The mannequin was a lesson. Real fights aren't. Whoever you face fights to win, the way you would; Health lost below the line stays lost, and anything you'd rather not be seen casting, someone may see. You can always refuse a fight, at a price of its own.
text [87f511] = 假人是一堂课。真正的打斗不是。你的对手会像你一样拼命想赢；生命掉到那条线以下就真的没了；你不想被人看见施放的东西，可能会被人看见。你总可以拒绝一场打斗，代价另算。
# en: A duelling hall with a real duel under way, two students circling, a third nursing a split lip on the bench.
scene [253250] = 决斗厅里正在进行一场真正的决斗，两个学生绕着圈，第三个在长椅上捂着破了的嘴唇。
# en: Nod and move on
opt.left.label [fd56d5] = 点点头走开
# en: You file it away. Somewhere in the hall, someone is losing well. Thorne would be pleased.
opt.left.say.1 [a76909] = 你记下了。厅里某处，有人正输得漂亮。索恩会高兴的。
# en: Watch a bout to the end
opt.right.label [a77d1e] = 把一局看完
# en: You watch two third-years fight to a standstill, bow and go to supper together. It looked like the opposite of a lesson. It was the same thing.
opt.right.say.1 [da1e9f] = 你看着两个三年级生打到僵持不下，鞠了一躬，一起去吃晚饭。看起来跟上课正相反。其实是同一回事。

@event jit_real_negotiation
# en: A Real Negotiation
title [a656f1] = 真正的交涉
# en: Not every talk is a quick word. Some are negotiations: someone across the table with reasons of their own, and something at stake. Charm, lore and guile all count, and so does how you come across today. The steward and her list were practice.
text [b69d87] = 不是每次谈话都只是一句话的事。有些是交涉：桌子对面的人有自己的理由，而且事关输赢。魅力、学识和诡计都有用，你今天给人的印象也有用。舍监和她的名单只是练习。
# en: A student and an official facing each other across a desk heaped with papers, both leaning forward.
scene [8e5ce0] = 一个学生和一位官员隔着堆满文件的桌子对坐，都向前倾着身子。
# en: Fair enough
opt.left.label [5ceb95] = 有道理
# en: You resolve to argue only with people who aren't holding a ledger.
opt.left.say.1 [5a9666] = 你决定以后只跟手里没拿账本的人争论。
# en: Remember the steward and her list
opt.right.label [38d6d1] = 记住舍监和她的名单
# en: However it went with the steward, the lesson was the same: the list was her whole argument. You make a note: always ask to see the line.
opt.right.say.1 [9228ea] = 不管和舍监那次结果如何，道理都一样：那份名单就是她全部的理由。你记下一条：永远要求看那一行。

@event jit_infirmary
# en: A Word From the Infirmary
title [7e8c40] = 医务室的叮嘱
# en: Sister Amaranth catches you on the stairs, looks at you once and steers you to a bed. "Low Health," she says. "Under thirty, the body starts to lose things it doesn't get back easily. Sleep. Eat. Stop fighting things." She doesn't believe you'll listen.
text [1c4072] = 阿玛兰斯修女在楼梯上拦住你，看了你一眼，就把你领到一张病床前。“健康太低了，”她说，“低于三十，身体就会开始失去一些不容易找回来的东西。睡觉。吃饭。别再跟东西打了。”她不相信你会听。
# en: A stern healer in a white apron writing on a chart at the foot of a student's bed.
scene [103642] = 一位严厉的治疗师系着白围裙，在学生床尾的病历上写着什么。
# en: Promise to rest
opt.left.label [cd2cf3] = 保证好好休息
# en: You promise. She writes it on your chart, which feels binding in a way promises usually don't.
opt.left.say.1 [190987] = 你保证了。她把它写进你的病历，这比一般的保证更有约束力。
# en: Ask how low is too low
opt.right.label [5ecf56] = 问多低才算太低
# en: "Lower than you are," she says, "is too low." She gives you a tonic that tastes of iron and disapproval.
opt.right.say.1 [f79c03] = “比你现在还低，”她说，“就太低了。”她给了你一瓶尝起来像铁和不赞成的补剂。

@event jit_something_more
# en: Something More
title [5acec4] = 不止如此
# en: You catch yourself looking for {x} in every room. That's new. Friendship grows on its own; this is something else, and it grows only when you let it. It can also go cold if you leave it too long.
text [6f22e2] = 你发现自己在每个房间里找{x}。这是新鲜事。友谊会自己生长；这是另一回事，只有你允许，它才会长。你放着不管太久，它也会冷下来。
# en: Two students in a crowded corridor, one of them looking back over their shoulder a moment longer than they meant to.
scene [1a1a5b] = 拥挤的走廊里两个学生擦肩而过，其中一个回头看得比本想的久了一点。
# en: Think about something else
opt.left.label [a1058f] = 想点别的
# en: You think about something else, with great determination, for almost an hour.
opt.left.say.1 [99e64e] = 你下定决心想别的事，坚持了快一个小时。
# en: Admit it, to yourself at least
opt.right.label [7b1c1d] = 承认吧，至少对自己
# en: You admit it to your pillow, which keeps it. Tomorrow you'll be braver. Possibly.
opt.right.say.1 [1d0022] = 你对枕头承认了，枕头替你保密。明天你会勇敢些。大概吧。

@event jit_rivals
# en: Rivals
title [9f39c8] = 对手
# en: Somebody here has decided you're the one to beat. A rival watches what you do and does it better, or tries to, and you'll find yourself doing the same. Rivals can soften into something else. They can also sharpen.
text [c8aff0] = 这里有人认定你就是要打败的那个人。对手盯着你做的事，然后做得更好，或者想做得更好，而你会发现自己也在这么做。对手可以软化成别的关系。也可以变得更尖锐。
# en: Two students passing on a staircase, neither giving way, both pretending not to notice the other.
scene [bba80b] = 两个学生在楼梯上相遇，谁都不让路，都假装没注意到对方。
# en: Ignore it
opt.left.label [e2ae0c] = 别理它
# en: You resolve to ignore it. You fail almost at once, which is how rivalry works.
opt.left.say.1 [596911] = 你决定不理它。几乎立刻就失败了，对手就是这么回事。
# en: Get better
opt.right.label [018f1f] = 变得更好
# en: You stay late in the library out of pure spite. It is extraordinarily motivating.
opt.right.say.1 [7df6b8] = 你纯粹出于赌气在图书馆待到很晚。这动力大得惊人。

@event jit_mirror
# en: The Mirror Remembers
title [a9c2e3] = 镜子记得
# en: You pass the Sorting Mirror on the way to breakfast and your reflection is a half-step slow. {alignment >= 15: It looks brighter than you feel.|It looks colder than you feel.} What you do when it costs you something is being remembered, somewhere, and it leans you one way or the other.
text [a31764] = 你去吃早饭时经过分院镜，镜中的倒影慢了半步。{alignment >= 15: 它看起来比你感觉的更明亮。|它看起来比你感觉的更冰冷。}你在付出代价时所做的事，正被某处记着，它会让你向这边或那边倾斜。
# en: A student passing the tall sorting mirror in the entrance hall, their reflection a half-step behind them.
scene [29c9fa] = 一个学生经过入口大厅那面高大的分院镜，倒影落后了他们半步。
# en: Walk faster
opt.left.label [ce8449] = 走快点
# en: Your reflection catches up by the end of the hall. You decide not to wonder how.
opt.left.say.1 [246381] = 到大厅尽头，倒影赶上了你。你决定不去想它是怎么做到的。
# en: Look back at it
opt.right.label [08174f] = 回头看它
# en: It looks back. Then it straightens its robes, which you hadn't, and you straighten yours.
opt.right.say.1 [3603d3] = 它也回看你。然后它整了整长袍——你还没整——于是你也整了整你的。

@event jit_noticed
# en: Noticed
title [15acef] = 引人注目
# en: Heads turn when you come into the common room. A first-year whispers your name to another. Being known opens doors and invitations; it also fades if you stop giving people something to talk about.
text [3d44cb] = 你一走进公共休息室，就有人转过头来。一个一年级生小声把你的名字告诉另一个。出名能带来机会和邀请；如果你不再给人们谈资，名声也会慢慢消退。
# en: A student walking into a crowded common room as a few heads turn, someone whispering behind a hand.
scene [1ff97c] = 一个学生走进拥挤的公共休息室，几个人转过头，有人用手挡着嘴说悄悄话。
# en: Pretend not to notice
opt.left.label [57b529] = 假装没注意
# en: You pretend not to notice. Everyone notices you pretending.
opt.left.say.1 [790a19] = 你假装没注意。所有人都注意到你在假装。
# en: Wave
opt.right.label [96ccf4] = 挥挥手
# en: You wave. Three people wave back, and one of them has no idea who you are.
opt.right.say.1 [d17e6b] = 你挥了挥手。三个人挥手回应，其中一个根本不知道你是谁。

@event jit_first_shift
# en: First Shift
title [11f651] = 第一次上班
# en: A job is a few shifts a term, shown on the map when they're due; each one pays, and a missed one costs the boss's good opinion. Work well and you're promoted. Turn up on a break and it's just a visit.
text [f01a2a] = 一份工作每学期要上几次班，该上的时候会显示在地图上；每次都有工钱，缺勤会让老板对你印象变差。干得好就能升职。假期去了就只算一次拜访。
# en: A student tying on an apron in a back room, a list of duties pinned on the wall beside them.
scene [84af70] = 一个学生在后屋系围裙，旁边墙上钉着一张职责单。
# en: Tie the apron and go
opt.left.label [22208f] = 系上围裙就去
# en: You tie the apron backwards. Nobody tells you for an hour.
opt.left.say.1 [a3b87d] = 你把围裙系反了。一个小时都没人告诉你。
# en: Read the duty list twice
opt.right.label [626776] = 把职责单读两遍
# en: You read it twice. The second time, you notice the line at the bottom: "Ask if unsure." You decide to be sure instead.
opt.right.say.1 [4ab7ca] = 你读了两遍。第二遍时，你注意到最下面一行：“不确定就问。”你决定干脆确定一点。

@event jit_applications
# en: Applications
title [7f7f22] = 申请
# en: The internship notices are up. A summer's placement means a summer away doing the work, and a letter from a supervisor that follows you after. Each wants a course passed, or more, and asks once a year.
text [1b9c79] = 实习的通知贴出来了。一个暑期实习意味着一个夏天在外面干活，还有一封之后会一直跟着你的导师推荐信。每个都要求通过某门课或更多，而且一年只招一次。
# en: A noticeboard plastered with internship notices, a student copying deadlines into a notebook.
scene [259d8b] = 贴满实习通知的布告栏，一个学生把截止日期抄进笔记本。
# en: Look later
opt.left.label [39e3b4] = 以后再看
# en: You walk past the board. The notices will still be there tomorrow, mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [c82002] = 你从布告栏前走过。那些通知明天大部分还会在那儿。
# en: Copy the deadlines down
opt.right.label [424d96] = 把截止日期抄下来
# en: You copy every deadline into your notebook in your best hand, and underline the ones you could actually meet.
opt.right.say.1 [2074de] = 你用最好的字迹把每个截止日期抄进笔记本，在你真能赶上的那几个下面划了线。
